## Journal Update

## What I worked on

This week I worked on the Quote Generator and focused on improving the functionality and user experience.

## What I changed

I added authentication for user accounts so users can securely create an account and sign in with their email address and password.

This provides a personalised experience where each user's saved quotes can be associated with their account.

## Why I made this decision

Previously, saved quotes were not tied to an individual user account. Authentication creates a foundation for persistent personalisation and allows users to access their saved content consistently.

## Users benefit

Users can create and access their own account.
Saved quotes are associated with the correct user.
Users can return to the application and continue accessing their saved quotes.
The experience feels more personalised and consistent.

## Reworked Category Navigation

I changed the category experience from having categories displayed directly within the navigation to using a dropdown menu.
## What I learned

## Why I made this change
Having every category displayed as part of the navigation could make the interface feel crowded and take up valuable navigation space.

The dropdown provides a cleaner way for users to discover and select different quote categories without overwhelming the main navigation.


## Next steps

Next step is to improve the user interface to be cleaner and easy to navigate
